course: dictionary
lesson: 289
title: Amphibians: animals of two worlds
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An amphibian is a cold-blooded animal with a backbone and moist skin. Most amphibians live part of their life in water and part on land. The word comes from ideas meaning "both", so it hints at living in two worlds. Frogs, toads, newts and salamanders are all amphibians.
explain: «Frogs, toads, newts and salamanders are amphibians; snakes, lizards, crocodiles and turtles are reptiles.» Both groups have backbones, but they belong to different groups of animals. Look for the clue words in the sentence to tell them apart.
explain: Amphibians often change as they grow. «Young amphibians usually live in water and breathe with gills; adults usually breathe with lungs and through their skin.» A young frog is a tadpole, and an adult frog is very different from it.
fact: An amphibian is one of five groups of vertebrates, with fish, reptiles, birds and mammals.
fact: The life cycle of a frog goes from egg (frogspawn), to tadpole with gills, to froglet, to adult frog with lungs.
fact: Amphibians must keep their skin damp, and they are sensitive to pollution, so they show how healthy an environment is.
fact: The Chinese giant salamander is the biggest amphibian in the world, and it lives in cold, fast streams.
fact: As a second meaning, an amphibian is a vehicle that can travel on both land and water.
exercise: «Frogs, toads, newts and salamanders are amphibians; snakes, lizards, crocodiles and turtles are reptiles.» Which of these is an amphibian? | Lizard | Snake | Turtle | *Newt
exercise: Which stage of a frog's life has gills for breathing? | Frogspawn | Adult frog with lungs | *Tadpole
exercise: «An amphibious vehicle can travel on land and ___.» Which word fits the gap? | Rails | Air | *Water | Snow
test: Amphi means both. Why does the word amphibian fit a frog? | It lives only in the sea | Frogs have fur and warm blood | *It lives part of its life in water and part on land | It never leaves the pond
test: Which animal is the biggest amphibian in the world? | Newt | Toad | Frog | *Chinese giant salamander
exam: Why do amphibians show how healthy an environment is? | They never leave the water | They are cheap to buy | They have feathers | *Their damp skin makes them sensitive to pollution
